t and drawing unflattering coverage; no public polls"], "rationale": "Colorado's Democratic lean, a six-outlet consensus of Solid or Safe Democratic ratings, and markets pricing Weiser near 96-97% all point to a comfortable Democratic hold on the open seat. Marx's competitive fundraising is undercut by rapid spending and critical coverage of his backstory, and no public polling suggests a closer race.", "watch": "A late poll showing single digits, a Weiser stumble in the remaining debates, or a conservative shift toward Lopez's independent bid could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Jared Polis (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Jared Polis is term-limited, leaving Colorado's governorship open, with Democrat Phil Weiser facing Republican nominee Victor Marx, a political newcomer. Independent Greg Lopez and a Libertarian are also on the ballot, adding minor wrinkles to the field.\n\nEvery available signal points the same direction. All six expert raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets put Weiser's chances near 96 to 97 percent. No public general-election polls exist, so expectations rest on Colorado's Democratic lean and the party's recent run of double-digit gubernatorial wins. Marx has kept pace with Weiser in fundraising but is spending quickly, and coverage of his personal backstory has turned critical. The race sits comfortably in the Democratic column, with modest residual uncertainty from the absence of polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9695, "margin": 12.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9677, "margin": 12.4}]}